TI  - Research on Music Course Teaching Resource Recommendation based on Convolutional Neural Network
PY  - 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICDSIS65355.2025.11070589
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105011815425&doi=10.1109%2FICDSIS65355.2025.11070589&partnerID=40&md5=415be170f1cbe65adbaa8eac1d053736
AB  - The fast development of online education calls for smart recommendation systems that can improve personalized music learning experiences. This paper introduces a Hierarchical Multi-Modal Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)-based recommendation model that can be specifically designed for the teaching resources of music courses. Current recommendation systems are plagued by low accuracy, poor contextual understanding, and limited adaptability to the distinctive auditory and structural properties of music-oriented data. Classic models like collaborative filtering and content-based ones tend to be ineffective in representing profound semantic relations between musical resources. However, the proposed architecture digs out hierarchical features from multi-modal music data (textual, audio, and visual inputs) to predict learner preferences accurately and provide relevant recommendations. Experimental results illustrate that the proposed model performs better than baseline models such as conventional CNNs and matrix factorization methods, reaching 94.2% accuracy and 93.5% F1-score, with superior performance in precision and recall trade-offs. The model's resilience and flexibility attest to its applicability in practical situations in dynamic learning environments, providing an intelligent and effective means for resource recommendation in music learning. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
