UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105008868942&doi=10.1016%2Fj.procs.2025.05.191&partnerID=40&md5=e81e8d6d6b6b7c8a90ab6365e846f130
AB  - Aiming at the core problems of online education in colleges and universities, such as unidirectional teaching, interactive asynchronism and evaluation linearity, this study proposes a deep learning-driven course recommendation system based on gated loop unit. By constructing a time-sensitive modeling framework for student behavior, the hierarchical attention mechanism and conversational interest extraction technology are integrated systematically and innovatively, breaking through the bottleneck of long-term dependence modeling of traditional recommendation models. At the level of algorithm design, GRU architecture is used to capture the dynamic learning track of cross-semester, and the adaptive integration of long- and short-term interests is realized through the collaborative control of update gate and reset gate. Experiments show that the AUC index of the proposed model is improved by 6.9%-7.5% compared with the traditional collaborative filtering algorithm and deep recommendation model, which verifies the effectiveness of time series modeling for feature extraction of educational data. Through B/S architecture and cognitive load optimization design, the system forms a closed-loop cognitive service system of "data acquisition - feature extraction - dynamic recommendation", which provides an innovative technical path for solving the quality dilemma of online education. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
