AB  - The value of the E-learning System in providing access to education for more people is rising rapidly. Positive effects on the learning process may be achieved via the use of the learner-centric approach and the Adaptive E-learning System (ALS). However, there are a number of obstacles to ALS research that need to be overcome using innovative approaches. One of the biggest obstacles facing ALS is finding ways to make education more effective for individual students. The learner's own preferences and habits, known as Learning Styles, should be taken into account in the design of this environment. However, the efficacy of learning may be increased by complementing the information with tailored advice, which isn't a primary emphasis of current learning systems. First, this paper presents a multi-agent architecture for ALS that use machine learning to personalize content delivery for individual students. Automated profiler, content indexer, and recommendation agent are the building blocks of the suggested system. The accessible electronic material is first gathered and identified in the system, and then the learner profile is established. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
