DO  - 10.1109/UEMCON62879.2024.10754751
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85212686874&doi=10.1109%2FUEMCON62879.2024.10754751&partnerID=40&md5=2103af637da33d8f01f8dfce5c6749e5
AB  - This paper introduces the Dynamic Strategy Optimizer (DSO), a novel hybrid approach that combines sampling with dynamic optimization to improve decision-making performance. The primary contribution is the DSO's ability to optimize multi-armed bandits (MAB) for higher rewards and significantly reduced computational time, outperforming traditional methods like Thompson Sampling, Epsilon Greedy, and A/B Testing. Additionally, we propose a novel hybrid recommender system (RS) architecture, scalable for large datasets, integrating collaborative filtering, neural network classification, and MAB techniques to address the cold-start problem in real-time recommendation systems. Evaluations on the MovieLens25m and JesterJoke1.7 datasets show that DSO achieves superior reward accumulation and computational efficiency, with times as low as 1.59 it / s on JesterJoke1.7 and 8.41 ~s / it on MovieLens25m, making it an efficient solution for large-scale adaptive systems. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
