AB  - In recent years, there has been huge growth in the use of online learning resources by learners. Since there is a huge amount of information available online, learners are experiencing difficulties in retrieving the exact learning resource that helps them to learn. There are a lot of drawbacks in the existing Recommender Systems and there is a need for a more accurate information. Most of the existing recommendation techniques do not consider differences in learner characteristics. A framework has been proposed for a Hybrid Recommendation System that uses Big Data and Deep learning to give accurate learning resources for the learners. Our approach involves the following steps: (1) Creating an Ontology for representing the learner's Knowledge, (2) Constructing a Framework that involves Big Data and Machine Learning, (3) Implementing a Module in Hadoop. The system will alleviate all the disadvantages and makes use of the latest available technology to recommend the most accurate information. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
